        "original_id": "038f1c0d-e68a-55fa-a448-d690c48d91cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Miami Dolphins, Kansas City Chiefs, New York Jets\n- People: Adam Gase, Andy Reid, John Dorsey\n- Events: 2016 Miami Dolphins season, 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season, Week 15 win, playoff berth, John Dorsey firing\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 Miami Dolphins season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League and its 51st overall season.\n- The 2016 Miami Dolphins season was the first under head coach Adam Gase.\n- In Week 15 of the 2016 season, the Miami Dolphins defeated the New York Jets to clinch their first winning record since 2008.\n- The Miami Dolphins clinched a playoff berth the following week.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League and its 57th overall season.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the fourth under head coach Andy Reid.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the fourth and final season under general manager John Dorsey.\n- John Dorsey was fired by the Kansas City Chiefs on June 22, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e898338e-58f7-5500-b78d-2ef285b8b0c0",
        "text": "The 2016 Miami Dolphins season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League, the 51st overall and the first under head coach Adam Gase, with their Week 15 win over the New York Jets, the Dolphins clinched a winning record for the first time since 2008, and clinched a playoff berth the following week after 2016 Kansas City Chiefs  47th season in the National Football League, the 57th overall and the fourth under head coach Andy Reid and the fourth and final season under general manager John Dorsey who was fired June 22, 2017.",
